.TH CAST-DESKTOP-GO 1 "October 2026" "cast-desktop-go 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cast-desktop-go \- stream Linux desktop and audio to Chromecast devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cast-desktop-go
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cast-desktop-go
is a high-performance utility for streaming the Linux desktop display and audio (X11 & PipeWire/PulseAudio) to Google Chromecast, Android TV, and Google Home smart speakers over low-latency HTTP Live Streaming with Fragmented MP4 (fMP4/CMAF).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart\fR
Start casting the desktop display and audio.
.TP
\fBstop\fR
Stop active casting session and return Chromecast to ambient backdrop.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Display current streaming status, device, uptime, and HTTP server URL.
.TP
\fBgui\fR
Launch the graphical interactive launcher dialog (KDE kdialog / Zenity).
.TP
\fBvolume\fR [\fI0-100\fR | \fI+N\fR | \fI-N\fR]
Get or set Chromecast TV volume level.
.TP
\fBmute\fR [\fItrue\fR | \fIfalse\fR | \fItoggle\fR]
Toggle or set Chromecast TV mute state.
.TP
\fBpause\fR
Pause Chromecast playback stream.
.TP
\fBplay\fR
Resume Chromecast playback stream.
.TP
\fBshortcuts\fR [\fIinstall\fR | \fIlist\fR | \fIremove\fR]
Manage global desktop keyboard shortcuts.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR [\fIget\fR | \fIset\fR | \fIshow\fR | \fIreset\fR]
Inspect or modify persistent configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-device\fR \fINAME|IP|INDEX\fR
Specify target Chromecast device.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-monitor\fR \fINAME|INDEX\fR
Capture a specific monitor in multi-head setups.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-window\fR \fITITLE|HEX_ID\fR
Capture only a specific application window.
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fIultra-low|balanced|cinema\fR
Latency optimization preset (default: balanced).
.TP
\fB\-\-hw-accel\fR \fIauto|vaapi|software\fR
Hardware video encoding acceleration (default: auto).
.TP
\fB\-\-audio-only\fR
Stream audio only for smart speakers.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-daemon\fR
Run casting session in the background.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
HTTP streaming server port (default: 8088).
